 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 7680,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first copied byte in the scene record is $07. The caller starts executing one byte later."
  },
  {
   "address": 7681,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Save and reload the caller stack pointer, install raster target $2BFD at line $FA and select multicolour bitmap mode in the bank at $4000. Initialize board state and choose a value for $2DFA from $24."
  },
  {
   "address": 7684,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Reload the saved stack, select raster line $FA and set bitmap mode with the bitmap at $4000 and matrix at $7C00. Clear the board-related state bytes and choose the initial $2DFA value from $24."
  },
  {
   "address": 7947,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sample the joystick, wait two CIA2 periods and call the board update routines. If the player is idle, use fire to start the path that sets $2DCC and requests sound $87."
  },
  {
   "address": 8017,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Clear the move timer $2D7E, set the busy flag $2D04 to $FF from zero, queue sound $83 and set $2D7F to 1."
  },
  {
   "address": 8036,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Update the board move and its timer. Return with a nonzero outcome after the thresholds on $2E72 and $2D7E are met while $2EB0 is set."
  },
  {
   "address": 8762,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Check the active board flags and timer. On timer expiry select a random nibble below nine for one coordinate and begin computing the other coordinate."
  },
  {
   "address": 9686,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Shift the sequences beginning at $2E74 and $2E8F by two and add the newest pointer pair and two position bytes at their heads."
  },
  {
   "address": 10261,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Select a six- or seven-step animation limit based on the chosen direction. Increment the pose step and clear the movement flag once it reaches the limit."
  },
  {
   "address": 10504,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Select the X offset and high-byte adjustment for the four possible directions, then initialize a four-sprite pose using that offset."
  },
  {
   "address": 10732,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Refresh the joystick. When a move can begin, check up, down, right and left in that order and store direction 0, 1, 2 or 3 in $2D05."
  },
  {
   "address": 11955,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "This scene record ends with the eleven byte marker copied by the unpacker at $0DDE."
  },
  {
   "address": 16384,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The first $400 bytes of the character-cell-ordered board bitmap at $4000. Each cell occupies eight bytes."
  },
  {
   "address": 17408,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Board bitmap cell bytes at offsets $0400\u2013$07FF, in the region selected by the clear bitmap-base bit of $D018."
  },
  {
   "address": 18432,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Pixels in board bitmap cells 256 through 383. The VIC combines them with the colours at $7C00 and in colour RAM."
  },
  {
   "address": 19456,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Board bitmap cells 384 through 511, stored starting at $4C00 in the active VIC bank."
  },
  {
   "address": 20480,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Bitmap cells 512 through 639. The bitmap rows use 40 such eight-byte cells."
  },
  {
   "address": 21504,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Pixels for board bitmap cells 640 through 767. Two bits select each multicolour pixel."
  },
  {
   "address": 22528,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Board bitmap cells 768 through 895, in the bottom part of the screen."
  },
  {
   "address": 23552,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The final 104 board bitmap cells. The bitmap ends at $5F3F after 1000 cells."
  },
  {
   "address": 24832,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Four 64-byte image slots selected by sprites 0\u20133 in the board play capture, with pointers $84 to $87."
  },
  {
   "address": 25088,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Two consecutive sprite masks copied to $6D00\u2013$6D7F by $230E, selected by the first branch of the knight pose selector."
  },
  {
   "address": 25216,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Alternative pair of sprite masks copied into the same sprite slots by $231B."
  },
  {
   "address": 25344,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Sixteen 64-byte pose records. This part of the bitmap bank matches the same pose records in The Ramps."
  },
  {
   "address": 26368,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Twelve sprite fragments for later player poses. The bytes of these slots match the ramp scene records."
  },
  {
   "address": 27776,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The 64-byte image selected by sprite 5 at the Phantom Knight play capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 27904,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Two 64-byte image slots selected by sprites 6 and 7 in the Phantom Knight play capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 28416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The upper bank of player fragments, with several blank slots around the start and visible limb masks in its later records. This range matches the ramp asset bank."
  },
  {
   "address": 29440,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Eight high sprite slots with additional movement and weapon silhouettes, byte-for-byte equal to the corresponding ramp shapes."
  },
  {
   "address": 29952,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The unpacked picture stream initializes $7500\u2013$76FF to zero. These bytes are still zero in the play capture."
  },
  {
   "address": 30464,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Lookup table for the colour RAM setup at $2C6B. The routine indexes it by the $7C00 screen matrix and substitutes 6 for $0E."
  },
  {
   "address": 31744,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The screen colour matrix begins at $7C00 because $D018 has high nibble $F. The final eight bytes also hold the sprite pointers."
  },
  {
   "address": 41845,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Repeated $08 bytes at $A375\u2013$A40F, after the input consumed by the scene picture decode."
  }
 ]
}